{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310584,"nonce":"h+rPeyffQF7mPUKpvTsCigJx5mU=","title":"switch-as-expression with `throw` in the default case emits a `Return` with no value despite a non-void return type — Cranelift backend ...","message":"**Status: UNFIXED at compiler level. Worked around in nue.**\n\n**Repro shape**:\n\n```haxe\npublic static function tensorByteSize(info:TensorInfo):Int {\n    var nElem = ...;\n    return switch (info.dtype) {\n        case 0: nElem * 4;\n        case 14: blockedSize(nElem, 256, 144);\n        case _: throw \"byte-size for dtype \" + info.dtype + \" not implemented\";\n    };\n}\n```\n\nCranelift backend errors:\n\n\u003e `Function 'tensorByteSize' has return type I32 but encountered\n\u003e Return with no value. This usually indicates missing lowering of\n\u003e method calls in the function body.`\n\n…and the function is replaced with a 4-byte `udf` trap stub (see\n`bugs_trap_stub_cascade`).\n\n**Root cause**: the lowering of `return \u003cswitch-as-expression\u003e` when\none case is divergent (throws / never returns) produces a `Return`\nMIR instruction with no value because the switch's merge phi\nexpects a value from every branch — but the throw branch has none.\nThe codegen sees a typed return but a value-less `Return`\ninstruction.\n\n**Workaround at the user level** — lift the throw out of the\nswitch:\n\n```haxe\nvar size = switch (info.dtype) {\n    case 0: nElem * 4;\n    case 14: blockedSize(nElem, 256, 144);\n    case _: -1;       // sentinel\n};\nif (size \u003c 0) {\n    throw \"byte-size for dtype \" + info.dtype + \" not implemented\";\n}\nreturn size;\n```\n\n**Compiler fix idea**: when lowering a switch-as-expression with a\ndivergent case body, either (a) omit that branch from the result\nphi entirely, or (b) emit a sentinel value path that's never read\nbecause the throw diverges. Probably (a) — the lowerer needs to\nnotice when a case body is divergent (Throw, Return, infinite-loop)\nand not feed its result through the merge.\n\nRelated: [[bugs_switch_with_let_field_scrutinee]] (the trailing-expr\nhoist for non-divergent case bodies — landed today),\n[[bugs_switch_expr_null_init]] (initial-value typing for the\nswitch result temp), [[bugs_trap_stub_cascade]] (the silent SIGILL\nthat surfaces this).\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_divergent_throw_in_switch_expr` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}